-- title:
--   Completed stalk of uv=wvarpi^E at a vertex point
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring which is a domain, let $\varpi \in O$ generate its maximal ideal, let $E \ge 1$ be a natural number, let $w \in O^{\times}$, and let $a \in O$ satisfy $a = w\varpi^{E}$. Consider the affine scheme `CrossingQuotient.crossingScheme a` $= \operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring `CrossingQuotient O a` $= O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - a)$, and let $m$ be a point of it whose stalk $B$ is a Noetherian ring and whose prime ideal `m.asIdeal` contains both of the distinguished elements `CrossingQuotient.U a` and `CrossingQuotient.V a` of `CrossingQuotient O a`. Write $\varphi$ for the identification of `CrossingQuotient O a` with the global sections of the scheme given by the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`, and compose it with the germ map at $m$ to land in $B$. Then there exist a complete discrete valuation ring $W$ which is a domain, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : O \to W$ with maximal ideal of $W$ generated by $\sigma\varpi$ and with $O \to W \to W/\mathfrak m_W$ surjective, and a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_B$-adic completion of $B$ onto `UVCrossingModel W ((σ ϖ)^E)` $= W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - (\sigma\varpi)^{E})$ (two-variable power series over $W$) such that: for every $o \in O$, $\iota$ sends the image in the completion of the germ of $\varphi$ applied to the image of $o$ to `UVCrossingModel.const ((σ ϖ)^E) (σ o)`, the class of the constant power series $\sigma o$; the image under $\iota$ of the germ of $\varphi(\mathrm{CrossingQuotient.U}\ a)$ equals `UVCrossingModel.U ((σ ϖ)^E)` times some unit of the crossing model; and the image under $\iota$ of the germ of $\varphi(\mathrm{CrossingQuotient.V}\ a)$ equals `UVCrossingModel.V ((σ ϖ)^E)` exactly.
--
--   This is the local model at a node: the completed local ring of the plane crossing $uv = w\varpi^{E}$ over a discrete valuation ring, at a point lying over the crossing, is the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV - (\sigma\varpi)^{E})$ over a complete discrete valuation ring $W$, with the identification normalised so that one coordinate goes to $V$ and the other to $U$ up to a unit. It is used to obtain the same description at an arbitrary étale chart, by transport along a flat local map inducing an isomorphism on residue fields.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_crossingScheme_uvCrossingModel_of_mem_asIdeal.lean

